FlowSense – Software Validation

Objective

To document the expected responses of the FlowSense irrigation controller before physical hardware testing.

Test Cases

Test| Input condition| Expected response
T1| Soil moisture above threshold| Irrigation OFF
T2| Soil moisture below threshold and tank sufficient| Irrigation requested
T3| Tank level drops and soil moisture rises| Irrigation verified
T4| Tank level drops but soil moisture barely rises| Possible leak or poor infiltration
T5| Tank level barely drops and soil moisture barely rises| Possible blockage or no delivery
T6| Invalid sensor reading| Sensor error; irrigation should stop
T7| Soil is wet and VPD is high| Irrigation remains OFF under the soil-moisture threshold rule
T8| Soil is dry and tank water is insufficient| Irrigation OFF; low-water warning

Status: Expected behaviors documented. These test cases have not yet been verified through hardware testing or a dedicated software simulation.
